Quick Start
1. Disable native Ollama (if installed)
If Ollama is running on your machine, it occupies port 11434 — stop it before launching Docker:
sudo systemctl stop ollama
sudo systemctl disable ollama
2. Start all services
docker compose up -d
Docker automatically handles:

installing Python dependencies (pip install)
setting up the environment (.env.example used directly)
downloading codestral and mistral into Ollama (first start only)

Verify everything is running:
docker compose ps
3. Ingest your database schema
# With the provided test schema:
docker compose run --rm ingest example.sql

# Or with your own schema:
docker compose run --rm ingest /app/my-schema.sql


# Ingest 
docker compose run --rm ingest.py calian_full_nodata.sql


