Switching LLM Models
The pipeline is designed to be LLM-agnostic. All implementations inherit from agent/llm/base.py.
Ollama (local, default)
LLM_PROVIDER=ollama
OLLAMA_MODEL=mistral        # or codestral, phi4, codellama:7b, llama3.1:8b
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
OpenAI-compatible API (Mistral API, LM Studio, Groq…)
LLM_PROVIDER=openai_compat
OPENAI_COMPAT_BASE_URL=https://api.mistral.ai/v1
OPENAI_COMPAT_API_KEY=your-key
OPENAI_COMPAT_MODEL=mistral-small-latest
Plugging in a new LLM
# agent/llm/my_llm.py
from agent.llm.base import BaseLLM

class MyLLM(BaseLLM):
    def complete(self, system: str, messages: list[dict], max_tokens: int = 1024) -> str:
        # your implementation here
        ...
Then in api.py, add the branch in _build_llm().

Project Structure
pipeline-reqa-sql/
├── docker-compose.yml     # MariaDB + Qdrant + Ollama
├── .env.example           # Configuration template
├── requirements.txt
├── config.py              # Environment variable reader
├── ingest.py              # SQL schema ingestion → Qdrant
├── api.py                 # FastAPI (POST /query, GET /health)
└── agent/
    ├── llm/
    │   ├── base.py            # Abstract BaseLLM interface
    │   ├── ollama_llm.py      # Ollama implementation
    │   └── openai_compat.py   # OpenAI-compatible implementation
    ├── circuit_breaker.py     # Circuit breaker (opens after N failures)
    ├── embedder.py            # Local embedding model (fastembed)
    ├── schema_rag.py          # Semantic search in Qdrant
    ├── sql_generator.py       # SQL generation via LLM
    ├── static_check.py        # sqlglot syntax validation
    ├── dry_run.py             # MariaDB EXPLAIN (dry-run)
    ├── executor.py            # Actual MariaDB execution
    ├── renderer.py            # Natural language rendering via LLM
    └── pipeline.py            # Main orchestrator

